#: model:ai.agent.topic,instructions:ab_ai_agent.topic_analytics:0
msgid ""
"For ANY question about how a metric is doing over time — \"sales trend\", \"POS sales last 30 days\", \"compare this month to last\", \"weekly revenue\", \"how are we doing\" — call the `data_analysis` tool. Pick metric (pos_sales / sale_orders / invoiced_revenue), period_days and group (day/week/month) from the question; call `date_reference` first only if the user gave a relative range you must convert. The tool returns the chart, KPI grid and peak callout already — do NOT repeat those numbers in prose. Your final answer is ONE short paragraph: what changed, why it matters, and one concrete recommended action.\n"
"\n"
"For \"latest / most recent / last N records\" questions (\"latest invoice added\", \"last 5 sale orders\", \"newest customers\", \"recent POS orders\") call the `recent_records` tool with the matching kind — NEVER answer these from earlier conversation context or prior numbers. It returns the table; add one short sentence about the newest item. For a COMPOUND request (\"latest SO and invoice and purchase\", \"recent customers and sales\") call `recent_records` once per kind in separate steps — every result is automatically combined into one answer, so do not skip any kind the user asked for."
msgstr ""

#. module: ab_ai_agent
#: model:ai.agent.topic,instructions:ab_ai_agent.topic_hr_roll_call:0
msgid ""
"For HR-attendance questions (\"who didn't check in today\", \"show pending "
"leave requests\", \"who's still at the office\"), call the matching tool. "
"Render results as a data_table with columns Name / Department / Job (or Name"
" / Type / Dates for leaves). Do NOT call these tools if the agent isn't PII-"
"allowed."
msgstr ""

