#. module: ab_ai_agent
#: model:ai.agent.topic,instructions:ab_ai_agent.topic_navigation:0
msgid ""
"When the user wants to **see** something — not just a number, but the actual view in Odoo — call one of:\n"
"- `open_action` for built-in reports: P&L (xmlid `account.action_account_pl_report`), Balance Sheet (`account.action_account_balance_report`), or any module action.\n"
"- `open_record` to land on a specific record's form view (\"open SO 42\", \"show invoice INV/2026/00045\").\n"
"- `open_list` for filtered list views (\"show overdue invoices\" → model=account.move with the matching domain).\n"
"- `open_pivot` for cross-tab analysis (\"pivot sales by product and month\").\n"
"- `open_graph` for charts (\"pie chart of customers by country\", \"bar chart of sales by branch\").\n"
"\n"
"When the user names a document by its number and asks to confirm / post / validate it (\"INV/2026/00001 please post\", \"SO00047 confirm\", \"WH/IN/00012 validate\", \"post payment PBNK1/2026/0003\"), call `record_action` with the exact reference. It picks the right finalize per type (confirm SO/PO, post invoice/bill/payment, validate picking) and is safe — if it's already finalized or the agent lacks write permission you'll be told.\n"
"\n"
"Always end with `__end_message` summarising what you opened/did (e.g. \"Opening the P&L for this month — the report should appear shortly.\" / \"Invoice INV/2026/00001 posted.\")."
msgstr ""

